@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Task: `skills_list` and `skill_view` tools (P09-08) Phase: 09 Owner: P09 slice B builder
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): `tools/skills_tool.py` (the list
+cache, the three disclosure levels, linked-file groups, required-variable handling and where the
+secret prompt is allowed). Closed before writing.
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): progressive disclosure. `skills_list` (level 0) gives one row per
+visible skill — name, description, category — and is cached per profile for 30 seconds (cleared
+at once by `skill_manage`). `skill_view(name)` (level 1) returns the whole `SKILL.md`, its parsed
+frontmatter and the support files the skill ships, grouped by folder. `skill_view(name, file_path)`
+(level 2) returns one support file; the path must still be inside the skill folder after symlinks
+are resolved. A skill can declare environment variables it needs: when one is missing and the
+session can ask a person for a secret (the local CLI answers `secret` server requests), the person
+is asked and the value is stored in the profile's secret store (they may skip). Surfaces that
+cannot answer (messaging) or must not wait (cron, one-shot, unattended) never ask; the result
+carries a setup hint pointing at the local CLI. Declared variables join the process passthrough set
+so sandboxed terminal and code runs receive them. Every view bumps `view_count`/`last_viewed_at`
+(P09-12) and records read evidence per (session, skill, file) with the content hash, which the
+review fork's write guard (P09-11) checks. Both tools are read-only (parallel-admissible).
+
+Inputs → outputs: `skills_list {category?}` → JSON `{skills: [...], count}`;
+`skill_view {name, file_path?}` → JSON `{name, path, content, metadata, linked_files, setup?}` or `{name, file_path, content}`; errors as `{"error": ...}`.
+
+Files: `src/indus/learning/skills/view_tools.py`, `tests/unit/learning/skills/test_view_tools.py`.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- unknown, ambiguous, disabled or broken skill → error naming the reason (ambiguous lists paths);
+- `file_path` with `..`, absolute, or a symlink leading out of the skill → refused;
+- support file missing → error listing the files that exist; binary file → size note, no content;
+- file larger than 1 MiB (external skills) → first 1 MiB with a cut note;
+- secret request unsupported / withdrawn / skipped → setup note, the view still succeeds;
+- telemetry failure never fails the view.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- the list cannot see the session's tool array (handlers are not given it), so `skills_list`
+  applies OS, environment, app and surface rules but not the tool/toolset conditions; the prompt
+  index (which knows the tools) applies all of them;
+- read evidence stores the sha256 of what was shown, so a file changed after the view is not "read";
+- the secret prompt goes through the P04 server-request broker (`secret` kind), never a direct
+  terminal prompt.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- list cache honoured within 30 s on an injected clock and refreshed after; category filter;
+- view of `SKILL.md`, a nested support file, `../` escape and symlink escape refused;
+- missing env var: fake broker answering `secret` stores the value; a broker raising
+  `RequestUnsupported` (gateway) gives the setup hint; cron context never asks;
+- view bumps `view_count`; disabled skill refused; read evidence recorded with the hash.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- `skills_list` ignores `requires_tools`/`fallback_for_tools` style conditions (see above); a later
+  seam could offer the session's tool names as a handler extra.
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened `tools/skills_tool.py`):
+- [x] 30 s list cache (test: `tests/unit/learning/skills/test_view_tools.py::test_list_cache_ttl`)
+- [x] linked files grouped by folder; level-2 path containment (test: `::test_view_nested_support_file`, `::test_escape_refused`)
+- [x] secrets asked only where a person can answer (test: `::test_missing_env_prompts_on_cli`, `::test_missing_env_hint_on_gateway`)
+- Deliberate differences: the reference resolves plugin skills through a separate path; ours go
+  through the same catalog. The reference also checks credential files; P09 has none.
+- Not taken: security warnings for project skills (P13).
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-19). Shared: none.
diff --git a/docs/notes/P09/skills-prompt-index.md b/docs/notes/P09/skills-prompt-index.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0282fc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/notes/P09/skills-prompt-index.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Task: Skills index in the prompt and mid-session delta (P09-07) Phase: 09 Owner: P09 slice B builder
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): `agent/prompt_builder.py`
+(`build_skills_system_prompt` and the helpers it calls: grouping, clipping, names-only categories),
+`agent/skills_index_delta.py` (all). Closed before writing.
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): the system prompt carries a compact "Skills" block so the model knows
+which procedures exist without loading them. Rows are grouped by category, each `- name:
+description` with the description clipped to 60 characters and a visible `…` when clipped (the
+model learns to view the skill for the rest). A coding posture can demote whole categories to one
+names-only line; nothing is ever dropped. Same-tier duplicates that cannot load by bare name get a
+one-line rename note instead of rows. The block is built once with the prompt and stays frozen
+(R07.29): a skill created, deleted or changed mid-session never rebuilds the prompt. Instead, each
+turn the index the prompt carries is compared with the index that would be built now; a change is
+announced once as a note on the next user message (the P04 note channel); the next compaction
+rebuild picks the change up in the prompt itself.
+
+Inputs → outputs: catalog + visibility (tools, toolsets, surface) + demoted categories → index
+text; `SkillsIndexBuilder(inner)` fills `BuildContext.skills_index` on every (re)build;
+`IndexDeltaTracker.note(prompt_text, current_index)` → note text or None;
+`stage_index_delta(notes, tracker, prompt, current)` stages it on the note channel.
+
+Files: `src/indus/learning/skills/prompt_index.py`, `tests/unit/learning/skills/test_prompt_index.py`.
+`src/indus/core/prompt/builder.py` already reserves `skills_index` in the volatile tier, so no
+change is needed there.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- no visible skills or no `skill_view` tool → empty block (the builder drops it);
+- description with newlines or runs of spaces → collapsed to one line before clipping;
+- exactly 60 characters → no mark; 61 → 59 characters + `…`;
+- plugin skills (`plugin:skill`) rows parse back correctly (split on `": "`, not `":"`);
+- a prompt rebuilt by compaction already lists the change → no note (and the tracker resets);
+- a skill added then removed before any compaction → a second note says the prompt list is
+  accurate again.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- block delimited by `<skills_index>` … `</skills_index>`, header and guidance in our own words;
+- one note per change in the difference; the note states the whole current difference;
+- the delta tracker lives on the session; a resumed session starts with an empty tracker, so its
+  first turn may repeat a note already in the transcript (cheap, and never wrong);
+- the builder wrapper is a `Builder` (P04 protocol), so the agent needs no new seam: the host passes
+  `AgentOptions.builder = SkillsIndexBuilder(PromptBuilder(), …)`.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- golden index for a fixture tree (categories, clipping mark, names-only demotion, duplicate note);
+- 60/61-char clipping; empty when the view tool is absent;
+- builder wrapper: prompt bytes unchanged after a mid-session add; next user message has exactly
+  one note, the following none; removal note; compaction rebuild lists the new skill.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- The per-turn call (`stage_index_delta` before each turn) and the builder wrapper are not wired into
+  `SessionService` here (that file is shared with slice A's memory block); it is a two-line seam:
+  pass `SkillsIndexBuilder` as `AgentOptions.builder` and call `stage_index_delta` with the
+  agent's `PromptLifecycle.notes` and `.prompt` before `run_turn`.
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened both files):
+- [x] 60-char clip with a visible mark (test: `tests/unit/learning/skills/test_prompt_index.py::test_clip_edges`)
+- [x] names-only demotion keeps every name (test: `::test_golden_index`)
+- [x] delta note once per change, prompt bytes unchanged (test: `::test_mid_session_add_and_remove`)
+- [x] rebuild includes the new skill and sends no stale note (test: `::test_compaction_rebuild_lists_new_skill`)
+- Deliberate differences: the reference reads the last delta back from the transcript for agents
+  rebuilt per turn; our sessions keep one agent, so the tracker is in memory only.
+- Not taken: safe-worker suppression (no safe worker yet), project-skill trust rows (P13).
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-19). Shared: none.
